SUMMARY:Transcription by Ben Lerner [OPTION 1]
DESCRIPTION:Novel Lovers of Sonoma County\, CA\nNamed a Best Book of the Y
 ear (So Far) by The New York Times.\n\n"Ben Lerner’s slender new novel\,
  “Transcription\,” is just 130 pages long\, yet it cracks open some of
  our most colossal and enduring philosophical questions." - NYT\n\n"I enth
 usiastically support this club discussing this very short work. The "plot"
 : the unnamed narrator\, who has a troubled home situation including a you
 ng daughter\, travels to Brown (not actually named) to interview the highl
 y influential aging polymath Thomas\, an intellectual namedropper and the 
 narrator's savior of sorts. Trouble is the narrator has killed his iPhone 
 and cannot record the interview. During the rambling interview which the n
 arrator pretends to be recording\, it appears Thomas is confusing his gues
 t with son Max\, one year behind the narrator and also with a young daught
 er problem. Next chapter is a Thomas celebratory seminar in which the narr
 ator admits he did not transcribe the "last" interview with Thomas but whi
 ch Thomas admirers have already used. Last chapter is the narrator seeing 
 the angry Max who did in fact record a last meeting with the dying Thomas.
 ..I thought the ending sublime....I won't share." - Ed\n\n"I can see why t
 his book received a lot of attention as it’s unconventional in its form 
 and writing style. This is not a ‘beach read.’ I appreciated the theme
 s of dependence on screens and how devices can bring us closer together an
 d alienate us. I also welcomed Lerner’s different views of how we parent
 ." - Lucinda\n\n"A short book filled with ideas to ponder and discuss: how
  our dependence on 'screens' both enables and limits our connection to oth
 er people\, how we understand our own histories and relationships\, how to
  raise a child who won't eat\, and much more. It's brainy and I do think i
 t will lead to good discussion." - Joan\n\nSee more comments and resources
  on our Discord!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/novel-lovers-of-sebastopol/events/315
 074710/
